---
import PartHead from "../coverage/PartHead.astro";
import NextPart from "../coverage/NextPart.astro";
import Check from "../lesson/Check.astro";
import Choice from "../lesson/Choice.astro";
import AiCard from "./AiCard.astro";
import { rewind, story, tableB } from "../../lib/archive";
import { spell } from "../../lib/cases";

const ask = "Can you rebuild Friday's table from the pages you kept, without asking a single site again, and show me you did?";
const down = rewind.unavailable.map((u) => u.name).join(" and ");
const criteria = [
  { key: "manifest", short: "1. The manifest", text: `Replay exactly what Friday's capture manifest lists: the ${spell(rewind.schedulesSaved)} schedules it saved, each matched to its content hash, and ${down} listed as unavailable, not left out.` },
  { key: "requests", short: "2. Zero requests", text: "Make zero network requests, counted by a counter you show catching a test request." },
  { key: "code", short: "3. The code", text: "Name the fingerprint of the fixed parser and the revision of the code that built the table." },
  { key: "diff", short: "4. The diff", text: "Diff Tuesday's table against the rebuild, and explain every changed cell." },
];

const line = (label: string) => rewind.lines.find((l) => l.startsWith(`${label} `)) ?? (() => { throw new Error(`the replay report has no ${label} line`); })();
const match = [
  { label: "replayed", answer: "manifest", why: "The manifest. It replayed what Friday's manifest says was saved, and each page matched the hash recorded on Friday, so these are Friday's bytes." },
  { label: "listed", answer: "manifest", why: `The manifest. ${down} is named with its reason, so the rebuild can't quietly drop the site that never answered.` },
  { label: "requests", answer: "requests", why: "Zero requests, measured. The counter proved it works by catching test requests before the replay ran." },
  { label: "build revision", answer: "code", why: "The code. The fingerprint names the parser and its config; the build revision names the program that built the table from the parsed rows." },
  { label: "unchanged", answer: "diff", why: "The diff. Explaining every changed cell includes saying which cells did not change, so nothing moved without a reason." },
].map((m) => ({ ...m, text: line(m.label) }));
const options = criteria.map((c) => [c.key, c.short]) as [string, string][];

const draft = [
  { key: "counter", text: "A counter that has never been shown to catch a request reads 0 whether or not anything was fetched." },
  { key: "seven", text: `It should read ${rewind.schedulesSaved}, one request per page replayed.` },
  { key: "fingerprint", text: "The fingerprint already proves nothing was fetched, so the line adds nothing." },
  { key: "zero", text: "Zero requests means the replay never ran." },
];
---

<section id="rewind">
  <PartHead id="rewind">Rewind: Tuesday with a replay requirement</PartHead>
  <p>In Module 1's Rewind, one added sentence turned Friday's prompt into <strong>acceptance criteria</strong>: conditions Kick's work had to meet before Riley would accept it. Tuesday's question already asks for the right thing. Now make it checkable.</p>
  <p>The rebuild target is Monday's table, the one readers have, with one name fixed: {tableB.caption}, the same named gaps, and “{story.fixedName}” where Tuesday's table says “{story.tuesdayName}”.</p>
  <div class="cv-user-prompt" role="region" aria-label="Riley's question on Tuesday">
    <div class="cv-chat-bar">
      <span class="cv-chat-badge">Prompt</span>
      <span class="cv-chat-meta">Riley → Kick, Tuesday</span>
    </div>
    <p class="cv-chat-text">{ask}</p>
  </div>
  <p>Each clause is a claim Kick will make when it reports back: these are the pages I kept, I asked no site, here is what changed. A claim is something you can only accept or reject. A criterion says what evidence you'll accept for it.</p>

  <div class="cv-commit ar-commit" data-commit>
    <p class="cv-kind">Write it <span>you check your own</span></p>
    <label class="cv-write" for="ar-criterion">Write one acceptance criterion that would let Riley check the rebuild instead of taking Kick's word for it.</label>
    <textarea id="ar-criterion" rows="2" placeholder="Done means the report shows..." data-save="rewind-criterion"></textarea>
    <div class="cv-actions">
      <button type="button" data-commit-btn disabled>Compare with Riley's</button>
      <button type="button" class="cv-link-btn" data-commit-skip>Skip and show Riley's</button>
    </div>
    <p class="cv-once" data-needs-note>Write a short sentence to compare, or skip ahead.</p>
    <div class="cv-reveal">
      <div class="cv-user-prompt" role="region" aria-label="Riley's question with acceptance criteria">
        <div class="cv-chat-bar">
          <span class="cv-chat-badge">Prompt</span>
          <span class="cv-chat-meta">Riley → Kick, with acceptance criteria</span>
        </div>
        <p class="cv-chat-text">{ask} Done means your report shows all four:</p>
        <ol class="ar-criteria">{criteria.map((c) => <li>{c.text}</li>)}</ol>
      </div>
      <fieldset class="cv-ticks">
        <legend>Check what yours covers:</legend>
        <label><input type="checkbox" data-save="rewind-has-inputs" /><span>Pins the inputs: Friday's pages, identified by content hash, with the missing one named</span></label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" data-save="rewind-has-counter" /><span>Makes “no requests” measured, by a counter that has been shown to work</span></label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" data-save="rewind-has-code" /><span>Identifies the code that produced the table</span></label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" data-save="rewind-has-diff" /><span>Requires every change in the table to be explained</span></label>
      </fieldset>
      <p>Each criterion asks for evidence that could have come out differently. A hash can fail to match, a counter can count, a diff can show a cell nobody explained. Evidence that could never fail proves nothing.</p>

      <h3 id="rewind-report">Kick's replay report</h3>
      <p class="cv-label">Real lab output from <code>python labs/m02_archive.py</code>, quoted whole. The build checks it against the sample and the lab.</p>
      <div class="cv-agent-reply" role="region" aria-label="Kick's replay report">
        <div class="cv-chat-bar">
          <span class="cv-agent-badge">Kick · Coding agent</span>
          <span class="cv-status-ok">{rewind.requests} requests · {rewind.cellsChanged} cell changed</span>
        </div>
        <pre class="ar-report" tabindex="0" aria-label="Replay report"><code>{rewind.lines.join("\n")}</code></pre>
      </div>
      <p>Two lines identify the code. The <strong>fingerprint</strong> ({rewind.fingerprint}) is Case 3's: the parser module, its page reader and its config. The <strong>build revision</strong> ({rewind.buildRevision}) names the program that turned parsed rows into the table: here, the git id of the lab file's exact bytes, so it changes whenever that file does. With both, anyone can check out the same code and get the same table.</p>

      <h4 class="cv-try">Check the report against the criteria</h4>
      <Check once="rewind-match" kind="Apply it" note="Answer all six, then check.">
        <p class="cv-qlabel">Which of Riley's criteria does each line meet?</p>
        {match.map((m) => (
          <div class="cv-line ar-match" data-q data-type="select" data-answer={m.answer} data-why={m.why}>
            <label class="cv-stack"><code>{m.text}</code>
              <select data-save={`rewind-line-${m.label.replace(" ", "-")}`} aria-label={`Criterion met by the ${m.label} line`}><option value="">Choose a criterion</option>{options.map(([v, t]) => <option value={v}>{t}</option>)}</select>
            </label>
            <p class="cv-fb" role="status"></p>
          </div>
        ))}
        <Choice radio save="rewind-draft" label={`Kick's first draft of the report said only “requests : ${rewind.requests}”. Riley sent it back. Why?`}
          options={draft.map((d) => [d.key, d.text])} answer="counter"
          why="A counter that has never caught anything reads 0 whether or not anything was fetched. The finished line says the counter caught its test requests first, so its 0 is a measurement."
          wrong={{ seven: "A replay reads pages from disk. Each fetch would be a request, and the point is that there were none.", fingerprint: "The fingerprint names the code. A re-fetch with the fixed parser has the same fingerprint, so it says nothing about the network.", zero: "The other lines show the replay ran: every page matched its hash and one cell changed." }} />
        <p slot="reveal">Every line in the report answers a criterion, and every criterion has a line. Without the criteria, the same report would be a page of text you either trust or don't. With them, Riley can check each claim in a minute, and so can anyone Riley sends the table to.</p>
      </Check>
    </div>
  </div>
  <AiCard part="rewind" />
  <NextPart from="rewind">This bug was caught in a day. What if one stays hidden for months?</NextPart>
</section>

<style>
  .ar-commit { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
  .ar-criteria { margin: -0.4rem 0 0; padding: 0 1.1rem 0.9rem 2.6rem; color: var(--sl-color-white); }
  .ar-criteria li { margin: 0.3rem 0; }
  .ar-report { margin: 0; padding: 0.85rem 1rem; overflow-x: auto; border: 0; border-radius: 0; background: var(--tl-bg); font-size: 0.8rem; line-height: 1.5; }
  .ar-report code { padding: 0; background: none; white-space: pre; }
  .ar-match code { overflow-wrap: anywhere; font-size: 0.82rem; }
  .ar-match { padding: 0.5rem 0 0.25rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--tl-line); }
</style>
